{"name":"Dear Darling","hex":"#a30112","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dear","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["High in price; expensive.","Loved; lovable."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very kind, loving person.","A beloved person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dear"},{"term":"darling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Often used as an affectionate term of address: a person who is very dear to one.","A person who is kind, sweet, etc., and thus lovable; a pet, a sweetheart; also, an animal or thing which is cute and lovable."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very dear; beloved, cherished, favourite.","Very cute or lovable; adorable, charming, sweet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/darling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Asami Imai","blocks":[{"text":"Asami Imai  is a Japanese voice actress and singer affiliated with Early Wing. She debuted as a voice actress in 1997 and as singer in 2009 by releasing her first single \"Day by Day / Shining Blue Rain\" under the 5pb. Records label. She is also well known for giving voices to Chihaya Kisaragi in The Idolmaster, Kurisu Makise in Steins;Gate, Tsubaki Yayoi in BlazBlue, and Ayumi Shinozaki in Corpse Party. She along with Eri Kitamura formed the music unit Artery Vein which is also under the 5pb. label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/Asami_Imai_-Officially_authorized_picture_for_Wikipedia-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asami_Imai"},{"title":"Mary Margaret O'Hara","blocks":[{"text":"Mary Margaret O'Hara is a Canadian singer-songwriter, actress, and composer. She is best known for the album Miss America, released in 1988. She released one album under her own name, a film soundtrack that she made with collaborators, and a Christmas EP. She remains somewhat active as a live performer, as a contributor to compilation albums and as a guest collaborator on other artists' albums."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Margaret_O'Hara"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"dear":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a4/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-dear.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a4/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-dear.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-dear.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a4/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-dear.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-dear.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-dear.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-dear.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-dear.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-dear.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-dear.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0f/En-us-dear.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/0f/En-us-dear.ogg/En-us-dear.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-dear.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wiki